      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The SCRIPPS trial is a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial evaluating the impact of gamma radiation to inhibit in-stent restenosis. Fifty-five patients were enrolled; twenty-six were assigned to receive catheter-based radiation with Ir-192 and 29 were treated with placebo. Angiographic restenosis in the Ir-192-treated patients was significantly reduced at six months (17% vs. 54%; p = 0.01), with the results sustained at 3-year follow-up (33.3% vs. 63. 6%; p<0.05). Likewise, the composite clinical endpoint of death, myocardial infarction or target lesion revascularization was also commensurately lower in the treated group as compared to the placebo group (23.1% vs. 55.2%; p = 0.01). Late angiography revealed no perforation, aneurysm or pseudoaneurysm or special safety issues unique to radiotherapy."},
